quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  2,270,"Whatever charity you may give, and whatever vow you may vow, Allah indeed knows it, and the wrongdoers shall have no helpers."
  2,271,"If you disclose charitable deeds (in public), that is fine, but if you hide them and give them to the poor (privately), that is better for you. It will atone for (some of) your misdeeds. Allah is All-Aware of what you do."
  2,272,"You are not responsible for their guidance. Rather, Allah guides whomsoever He wills. Whatever wealth you spend (in charity) is for your (own) benefit, as long as you spend only to seek Allah’s pleasure. And whatever wealth you spend (in charity) shall be repaid to you in full, and you will not be wronged."
  2,273,"(Charity is) for the needy wholly occupied in the way of Allah, not capable of moving about in the land (for trade). The ignorant (of their position) consider them to be wealthy because of their abstinence (and modest behaviour). But you recognise them by their characteristic; they do not ask the people importunately. And whatever wealth you spend—indeed Allah is All-Knowing of it."
  2,274,"Those who spend their wealth (in charity) by night and day, secretly and openly—for them is their reward with their Lord; there shall be no fear on them, nor shall they grieve."
